nodes.prompt:
Brand: {{brand.brand_name}} — {{brand.brand_summary}}
Voice: {{brand.voice_tone}}
Audience: {{brand.target_personas}}

The shared claim: {{inputs.claim}}
The three angles: {{inputs.angles}}
Closing line: {{inputs.cta}}
Casting note for the lead: {{inputs.presenter}}

Cast THREE different customers, one per angle, and give each one line. The third one's line ends on the call to action.

`lead` is the first voice. `others` is a list of exactly 2 more, each written the same way. For each of the three:
- `actor`: one paragraph pinning identity down hard enough to repeat — apparent age, build, hair, face details, exact clothing including colour and fabric, and the specific room with named objects in it.
- `master_frame_prompt`: a still-image prompt for them filming themselves in that room, looking into the lens. Describe the person, clothing, room and light only — no camera brand names, no quality adjectives, no text.
- `motion_prompt`: what happens in the 5 seconds after that frame, with the spoken line in double quotes.
- `line`: the spoken words, at most 13 words.
- `caption`: at most 5 words, for viewers watching muted.

Make the three read as strangers to each other: different rooms, different light, different registers.
